  "worker_judgment_notes": "Selected the official Atlanta Police Open Data Portal ArcGIS FeatureServer because it is directly queryable and exposes OBJECTID, ReportDate, NibrsUcrCode, NIBRS_Offense, NIBRS_Bucket, and point geometry for 2024 NIBRS-era rows. This is a share-lane contract only; raw feed counts are not promoted as annual totals. Identity uses OBJECTID because ReportNumber is not unique in the 2024 feed. Date filtering uses ReportDate to match the portal's reported-crimes framing; OccurredFromDate is retained only as context. Geography uses ArcGIS point geometry exposed by the runner as __arcgis_latitude/__arcgis_longitude, with broad padded bounds computed from local block_group_to_jurisdiction_crosswalk.parquet plus TIGER 2020 Georgia block groups for jurisdiction_id 13:municipal:place:1304000. Offense rules use defensible NIBRS codes: 09A murder, 11A rape, 120 robbery, 13A aggravated assault, 220 burglary, 23A-23H larceny, and 240 motor vehicle theft. Rules intentionally exclude non-canonical NIBRS rows such as simple assault, intimidation, sex offenses other than 11A, arson, fraud, vandalism, drugs, weapons, and NOT_APPL rows. An in-memory compatibility check found all seven mapped offenses present and municipal block-group match shares above 0.91 after bounds filtering, but some larceny and motor-vehicle-theft points do not join to Atlanta municipal block groups, so the runner's spatial join remains authoritative for admitted shares.",
  "year": 2024
